{"kind":"notes","id":"nt/3rsdza","slide":4,"text":"Lifecycle: after authentication the student submits a category, precise location, description and optional photo. Validation failures return to the form. A valid complaint begins as Submitted. The admin reviews urgency and assigns an appropriate staff member, producing Assigned status. Staff mark In Progress and then Resolved with completion notes. The student confirms the repair and rates it, producing Closed. If the issue remains, the student reopens it and the admin can reassign work. The sequence focuses on the submission and assignment scenario; database acknowledgements are omitted for readability. Admin and Staff share a diagram lifeline to show the management interface, but retain separate permissions."}
